	"nodes":[
		{
			"id":"f721070fb0e10c6c",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"text":"# Refractive Index\nThe index of refraction of a material is defined as the ratio between the velocity of light in vacuum and in the material\n$$n = \\frac{c_{0}}{c}=\\sqrt{ \\frac{\\epsilon \\mu}{\\epsilon_{0}\\mu_{0}} }$$\nfor nonmagnetic materials $\\mu_{0}=\\mu$ and so\n$$n = \\sqrt{ \\frac{\\epsilon}{\\epsilon_{0}} }=\\sqrt{ 1+\\chi }$$\n\n",
			"type":"text",
			"x":800,
			"y":40,
			"width":440,
			"height":420
		},
		{
			"id":"a1da8a5e70529058",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"text":"# Poynting Theorem\nThe Poynting vector (Energy Flux) of electromagnetic field is\n$$\\mathbf{S}=\\mathbf{E}\\times \\mathbf{H}$$\nTaking the divergence of \n$$\\begin{align}\n\\nabla \\cdot \\mathbf{S}  & = \\nabla \\cdot(\\mathbf{E}\\times \\mathbf{H}) \\\\\n&=\\mathbf{H}\\cdot(\\nabla \\times \\mathbf{E})-\\mathbf{E}\\cdot(\\nabla \\times \\mathbf{H}) \\\\\n&=\\mathbf{H}\\cdot\\left( -\\frac{ \\partial \\mathbf{B} }{ \\partial t }  \\right)-\\mathbf{E}\\cdot\\left( \\frac{ \\partial \\mathbf{D} }{ \\partial t } +\\mathbf{J}_{free} \\right)\n\\end{align}$$\nRecall that the energy density of electromagnetic fields in materials is given by the following expression\n$$ u = \\frac{1}{2}\\Big[\\mathbf{E}\\cdot \\mathbf{D}+\\mathbf{H}\\cdot \\mathbf{B}\\Big] $$\nFor time-independent permittivity and permeability the above can be simply written as\n$$-\\frac{ \\partial u }{ \\partial t } =\\nabla \\cdot \\mathbf{S}+\\mathbf{J}\\cdot \\mathbf{E}$$\nthe decrease in energy density in a point is due to energy flowing away from there (divergence of Poynting vector) and conversion of EM energy to mechanical energy (due to Lorentz force).",
			"type":"text",
			"x":1320,
			"y":-380,
			"width":580,
			"height":820,
			"color":"3"
		},
		{
			"file":"2. Notes/Poynting Theorem.md",
